WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.842
Coding Exercise 2 combines text normalization with fallback logic.

00:00:04.842 --> 00:00:11.022
Your goal is to produce the first usable contact value in this priority order: email, mobile phone,

00:00:11.022 --> 00:00:13.152
home phone, then No contact provided.

00:00:13.152 --> 00:00:18.922
Do not use COALESCE directly on the raw fields.

00:00:18.922 --> 00:00:22.287
Remember that empty text and whitespace-only text are still non-NULL.

00:00:22.287 --> 00:00:30.812
For each contact field, trim the text and use NULLIF to convert an empty cleaned value to NULL.

00:00:30.812 --> 00:00:33.452
Then place those normalized expressions inside COALESCE.

00:00:33.452 --> 00:00:41.447
When you run the query, inspect the edge cases instead of only checking whether the exercise passes.

00:00:41.447 --> 00:00:45.852
A patient with spaces in the email field should fall back to mobile.

00:00:45.852 --> 00:00:49.877
A patient with no email or mobile should use home phone.

00:00:49.877 --> 00:00:55.142
A patient with no usable contact information should receive the final label.

00:00:55.142 --> 00:01:01.412
This exercise represents a common real-world data-preparation task: standardize first,

00:01:01.412 --> 00:01:03.205
then apply business priority.
